e  affected northern areas is now  restricted except for emergencies and  legitimate health and work reasons and  those still in the region around 16  million people are being told to stay  indoors as much as possible but look as  the Chilean donnell imagine that what is  happening in my city is worrying me and  this is also sad because Milan is a  lively city and to see it like this  today is almost a defeat for me we have  to remain positive and calm and live in  the best way taking all precautions we  have to adapt our lifestyles but we  carry on the government has said anyone  found flouting the ban could face jail  but patrolling the region to ensure  everyone stays put will be another  challenge for a government dealing with  Europe's worst coronavirus crisis  Michelle Clifford Sky News Rome
 

